            <ArticleTitle>Care of the Elderly Patient on Oral Oncolytics for Advanced Disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>233-239</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s13670-016-0183-8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Oral oncolytics are now a common component of cancer care for older individuals with advanced cancer when a new treatment regimen is needed. Many of the solid tumors in elderly patients may respond to the oral oncolytics, however not without side effects and challenges to maintain adherence. This article describes some of the important areas to be considered when oral oncolytics are prescribed for elderly patients. A general overview of important intervention areas of focus is included.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
